{
  "id": "XIHSFNIAN",
  "name": "StreamProcessingFundamentals",
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "text": "\n**Input Sources:**  \n- Apache Kafka\n- File on distributed file system like hdfs, s3, deta lake\n- a socket source for testing\n**Output Sources:**\n-  apache kafka\n- almost any file format\n- a foreach singk for running arbitary computaiton on th output records\n- a console sink for testing\n- a memory sink fo rdbugging\n\n**Output Modes**\n- Append : only add new records to the output sink\n- update: update changed records in place\n- complete : rewrite the full output\n\n**Triggers**:*Whereas output modes define how data is output, triggers define when data is output*\n- look for new data at fixed interval,save us hitting sink many times\n\n**Event-Time Processing**\n- Structured Streaming also has support for event-time processing (i.e., processing data based on\ntimestamps included in the record that may arrive out of order)\n\n**Watermarks**\n- Watermarks are a feature of streaming systems that allow you to specify how late they expect to\nsee data in event time. For example, in an application that processes logs from mobile devices,\none might expect logs to be up to 30 minutes late due to upload delays",
      "config": {
        "colWidth": 12,
        "fontSize": 9,
        "enabled": true,
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/markdown",
        "editorSetting": {
          "params": {},
          "forms": {},
          "language": "markdown",
          "editOnDblClick": false,
          "completionKey": "TAB",
          "completionSupport": true
        }
      },
      "settings": {
        "params": {},
        "forms": {}
      },
      "id": "4f50227779cc464c98c18"
    },
    {
      "text": "%sql\nselect * from device_counts;",
      "config": {
        "colWidth": 12,
        "fontSize": 9,
        "enabled": true,
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/sql",
        "editorSetting": {
          "params": {},
