      "id": "01eb94b9fa01464ea4bd0"
    },
    {
      "text": "%spark\n//Now that we set up our transformation, we need only to specify our action to start the query\n//output sink\n//we use the complete output mode. This mode rewrites all of the keys along with their counts after every trigger in form of memory table, so we can query it below\nval activityQuery = activityCounts.writeStream.queryName(\"activity_counts\")\n.format(\"memory\").outputMode(\"complete\")\n.start()\n\n//You’ll notice that we set a unique query name to representthis stream, in this case activity_counts",
      "config": {
        "colWidth": 12,
        "fontSize": 9,
        "enabled": true,
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/scala",
        "editorSetting": {
          "params": {},
          "forms": {},
          "language": "scala",
          "editOnDblClick": false,
          "completionKey": "TAB",
          "completionSupport": true
        }
      },
      "settings": {
        "params": {},
        "forms": {}
      },
      "id": "7544b6d144e64969a843e"
    },
    {
      "text": "#### What is Streaming ?\nStream processing is the act of continuously incorporating new data to compute a result. In\nstream processing, the input data is unbounded and has no predetermined beginning or end\nsimply forms a series of events that arrive at the stream processing system (e.g., credit card\ntransactions, clicks on a website, or sensor readings from Internet of Things [IoT] devices)\n\n1. DStreams API : mr rdd\n2. Structure Api: super set fo DStreams,will often perform better due to code generation and the Catalyst\noptimizer\n\n\n#### Stream vs Batch\n0. Batch processing computation runs on a\nfixed-input dataset. Oftentimes, this might be a large-scale dataset in a data warehouse that\ncontains all the historical events from an application (e.g., all website visits or sensor readings\nfor the past month). Batch processing also takes a query to compute, similar to stream\nprocessing, but only computes the result once\n\n0. they often need to work\ntogether. For example, streaming applications often need to join input data against a dataset\nwritten periodically by a batch job",
      "config": {
        "colWidth": 12,
        "fontSize": 9,
        "enabled": true,
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/markdown",
        "editorSetting": {
          "params": {},
          "forms": {},
          "language": "markdown",
          "editOnDblClick": false,
          "completionKey": "TAB",
          "completionSupport": true
        }
      },
      "settings": {
        "params": {},
        "forms": {}
      },
      "id": "d8b2acbbeec042d59c179"
    },
    {
      "text": "####Stream Processing Use Cases\n\n0. Notifications and alerting\n0. Relea-time reporting\n0. Incremental ETL\n0. update data to serve in real time:  captuing click on web\n0. Rel-time decision making: \n0. Online machine learning\n",
      "config": {
        "colWidth": 12,
        "fontSize": 9,
        "enabled": true,
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/markdown",
        "editorSetting": {
          "params": {},
          "forms": {},
          "language": "markdown",
          "editOnDblClick": false,
          "completionKey": "TAB",
          "completionSupport": true
        }
      },
      "settings": {
        "params": {},
        "forms": {}
      },
      "id": "8047dbbcae3a46fcbfdde"
    },
    {
      "text": "%spark\nval historicalAgg = static.groupBy(\"gt\", \"model\").avg()\nval deviceModelStats = streaming.drop(\"Arrival_Time\", \"Creation_Time\", \"Index\")\n.cube(\"gt\", \"model\").avg()\n.join(historicalAgg, Seq(\"gt\", \"model\"))\n.writeStream.queryName(\"device_counts\").format(\"memory\").outputMode(\"complete\")\n.start()",
      "config": {
        "colWidth": 12,
        "fontSize": 9,
        "enabled": true,
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/scala",
        "editorSetting": {
          "params": {},
          "forms": {},
